WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.834
Federal officials have

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.135
been working around the clock

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.770
to try to find some resolution

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.771
in the wake of the collapse

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.106
of Silicon Valley Bank.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.073
And tonight,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:07.540
the Treasury

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.642
Department, FDIC and Federal Reserve,

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.311
all releasing a statement

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.413
saying that all depositors

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.848
with money at Silicon

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.483
Valley Bank will be made whole.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.318
That includes the depositors

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.486
who previously

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.756
they're depositors only up to $250,000

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.990
had been insured.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.025
Additionally,

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.993
they also announced that a second bank

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.162
signature bank has also been closed.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:29.963
I want to read you

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.164
a bit of this statement

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.899
which said that after consultation

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.768
with the FDIC, the Federal Reserve

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.369
and also President Biden

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.604
quote, Secretary Yellen

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.939
approved actions enabling the FDIC

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.474
to complete its resolution

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.675
of Silicon Valley Bank,

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.410
Santa Clara,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.911
California, in a manner

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.047
that fully protects all depositors.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.715
Depositors will have access

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.682
to all of their money

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.718
starting Monday, March 13th.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:52.652
No losses

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.987
associated with the resolution

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.188
of Silicon Valley Bank

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.090
will be borne by the taxpayer.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.491
The statement goes on to say,

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.427
They are extending the same protections

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.128
to those depositors with money,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.163
a signature bank,

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.798
which is based in New York.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.665
And additionally,

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:06.299
they said that

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.301
shareholders and certain unsecured

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.470
debt holders will not be protected,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.205
nor will be senior management

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.239
at this company.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.174
This comes

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:14.507
as they have

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.208
really been trying

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.777
to seek this resolution to the issues

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.712
that depositors are facing in the wake

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.313
of the closing

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.181
of Silicon Valley

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.350
Bank, about 90% of depositors

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.454
had money over $250,000,

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.688
which was the previous limit

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.256
that the FDIC insured,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.958
leaving many questioning

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.259
what exactly they would do

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.061
and how payroll would be met

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.362
heading into this week.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.464
Now we are still waiting to get

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:38.465
some more specifics

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.233
from the Treasury Department

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.302
and other regulators here in Washington.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.703
But it comes at a time,

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.537
as they have been working

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.606
very closely on this matter,

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.541
trying to prevent any further

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.543
jitters that it could

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.545
cause for the banking system and the U.S.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.079
economy.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.814
I will note in this statement,

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.083
they also try to stress the resilience

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.885
of the banking system in this moment,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.854
in part based on those protections

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.921
that were regulations

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.323
that were put in place

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:06.025
after the financial crisis in 2008.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:06.693
All right. Our right.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.660
Thank you very much.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.128
And CNN

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.963
economics and political commentator

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.065
Catherine Rampell is back with us.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.166
Catherine, your reaction

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.700
to this statement?

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.068
I'm just looking at what the

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:15.902
this joint statement

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.837
that came out from the treasury secretary

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.739
the Federal Reserve chair

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:20.874
and the FDIC chairman.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.242
It also mentions,

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.344
as Arlette was saying, signature bank

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.745
and so on

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.847
at the close of business on Friday.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.817
We had heard about Silicon Valley Bank.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.952
Now we're hearing about a second bank

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.921
that is obviously going to

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.022
cause some concern

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.724
that some of this is spreading

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.626
and that this is becoming a larger issue.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.495
Yes, there were a number of banks

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.164
that saw their stock prices

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.698
tank on Friday

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.300
as a result of concerns

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.968
about Silicon Valley Bank.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.170
People were worried, well,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:50.904
that happen there.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.139
Maybe it can happen here as well.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.607
I've also heard lots of reports

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.074
about people

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:55.808
pulling their money

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:56.910
out of a range of other

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.411
kind of comparable,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.812
mid-sized, mid

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.649
mid to large sized regional banks

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.118
that didn't necessarily

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.720
exhibit any signs of stress prior

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.454
to all of this.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.756
It's this sort of contagion,

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.958
this financial panic contagion.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.660
And which is why

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.296
precisely why the administration

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.730
and the federal Reserve

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.565
were keen

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:21.568
on making sure that they stopped

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.502
the panic here

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.703
before it spread

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.405
to other financial institutions.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.172
And I think that's

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.941
what they're hoping happened here,

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.175
that the depositors

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.109
at Silicon Valley

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.010
Bank and its signature

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.178
bank are being told

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.479
that they will be made whole.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.582
There apparently wasn't a buyer

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.616
for Silicon Valley Bank,

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:38.151
despite the request for bids,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:38.985
or at least nothing

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.753
that's been announced so far.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.190
But the FDIC, in conjunction

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.692
with the Federal Reserve

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.026
and the Treasury Secretary,

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.795
apparently determined that there would be

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.997
what's called a systemic risk exception

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:52.599
and that they would make sure

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:54.267
that that the government essentially

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.501
would make sure

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.471
that those who had deposits at Silicon

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.506
Valley Bank would be made whole.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.275
Normally, again,

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.143
the FDIC only insures

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.446
deposits up to $250,000.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.580
That was not the case

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.082
of many of the deposits.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.083
Many of the accounts

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.584
at this bank exceeded

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.419
far exceeded that level.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:17.657
So the idea here is to calm that concern,

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.760
calm the concern of any depositors

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.062
at comparable banks

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.597
so that they don't

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.765
that that sort of panic

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.267
doesn't feed on itself.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.568
That's the goal here.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:28.868
Right.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.670
And Catherine, just a quick follow up.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.237
We're looking at

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.539
what it looks like

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.741
we're going to be seeing

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.808
on Wall Street tomorrow.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.277
Morning, the Dow futures,

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.512
NASDAQ futures, S&amp;P. 500 futures.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.613
They don't appear

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.315
to be spooked at this point,

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.750
but we know that there are jitters

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.852
and concerns that some of this may.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:46.352
I mean,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.220
I think Maxine Waters

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.821
was using the word contagion earlier

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.223
when we were talking to her

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.491
earlier on in this hour,

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.493
that this may lead to more fear

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.560
and loathing on Wall Street.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.194
But at this point,

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.129
we're not really seeing that

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.330
at this point.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.699
Well, I think the hope was that

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.667
in some sense,

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.601
the feds would step

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.869
in, whether that meant

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:05.204
finding another buyer, whether that meant

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.240
relaxing access

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.841
to the Fed's lending window,

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.510
which they also did,

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.046
or whether that meant stepping in

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.147
and essentially

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.682
having the government

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:18.151
guarantee that all of the deposits

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:18.518
at these

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:19.552
couple of banks

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:22.055
would be fully accessible tomorrow

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.589
in their entirety,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.591
not just weeks from now.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.360
Up to $200,000

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.028
or after all of this was sorted out, etc.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:31.030
That's why there was a lot of concern.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.733
So now that the government has stepped in

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.436
and tried to provide a resolution

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:37.503
that may be calming

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.005
some of those jitters,

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.074
I don't know if it'll be sufficient

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.042
because they've only announced it

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.177
for these two banks.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.211
The question is

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.613
how do investors, how do depositors

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.282
extrapolate to other banks?

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:50.583
Do they say, aha,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.117
if the

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:54.120
if the FDIC and Treasury and the Fed

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.755
were willing to

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:57.223
stop the

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.157
panic, stop the

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.459
bleeding at this one bank,

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.327
will they do it at my bank as well?

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.795
And we don't know yet

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.564
how that will be interpreted.

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:05.965
I'm sure I'll be looking, as others

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.533
will, at markets tomorrow

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:08.234
and at behavior

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.436
at these financial institutions tomorrow.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:11.637
Absolutely.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.506
If folks are lining up at the bank,

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:15.308
that that might be a sign

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:16.676
of where things might be heading.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:18.444
Our Catherine Rampell, thank you so much.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.078
We appreciate it.

